-- ============================================================================
-- supply ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Terminals, Depots & Fuel Supply, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE TANK AND THE DAY. Everything starts from a dip read
-- off a tape; a strapping table turns a height into a volume, linear between
-- two entries and silent outside its own range; free water is converted
-- through the same table and taken off; a VCF turns a gross observed volume
-- into a standard one, and its coefficients are an input the engine never
-- ships; and the day closes from yesterday's closing stock, with the gap
-- judged against a tolerance on what moved.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A missing value stays missing. No dip, no
-- table entry, no coefficient and no opening stock is ever read as a zero,
-- and each is refused in the engine's own words.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A reconciliation whose opening stock is taken
-- from today's own dip balances every day, so it measures nothing. The gap is
-- the point of the day.
--
-- HELD, taught as a limit and never graded: the VCF coefficient tables are a
-- published table the engine does not ship (FINDINGS-supply H2); the course
-- shows the form on SYNTHETIC coefficients and corrects its stocks with a VCF
-- typed off the terminal's own tables. The capstone grades six volumes in m3,
-- each to two decimals, at a tolerance of 0.01 m3.
-- ============================================================================

values ('supply', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-terminal-measures","title":"What a Terminal Measures","lesson_keys":["l01-two-apps-and-one-chain","l02-everything-starts-from-a-dip","l03-missing-stays-missing","l04-what-the-engine-will-not-ship"]},{"key":"m02-the-strapping-table","title":"The Strapping Table","lesson_keys":["l01-a-table-of-heights-and-volumes","l02-between-two-entries","l03-below-the-first-entry","l04-above-the-last-entry","l05-a-horizontal-tank-and-its-curve"]},{"key":"m03-free-water-and-the-gross-volume","title":"Free Water and the Gross Volume","lesson_keys":["l01-water-under-the-product","l02-the-water-cut-through-the-same-table","l03-a-water-cut-the-engine-refuses","l04-the-gross-observed-volume"]},{"key":"m04-the-volume-correction-factor","title":"The Volume Correction Factor","lesson_keys":["l01-a-litre-grows-when-it-warms","l02-the-form-of-the-correction","l03-the-coefficients-are-an-input","l04-a-vcf-read-off-your-own-table","l05-the-standard-volume"]},{"key":"m05-closing-the-day","title":"Closing the Day","lesson_keys":["l01-opening-plus-receipts-less-deliveries","l02-no-opening-stock-no-day","l03-a-reconciliation-that-cannot-fail","l04-tolerance-on-what-moved","l05-a-run-in-one-direction"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-akodo-tanks-end-to-end","l02-the-akodo-day-end-to-end","l03-what-the-next-tier-changes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
